  "term": "moral judgment",
  "definition": "Moral judgment is an evaluation of the ethical quality of a person's conduct or character. In a broader historical sense, it can also mean a value judgment that appraises what is fitting or worthwhile by reference to some standard or ideal, rather than simply what is true.",
